      'Setup example: 4 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Achieve the lowest total score in your 4-card layout by the end of the round.',
      "Turn-flow example: Turn: draw from stock or top discard. Use drawn card to (a) replace one face-down layout card without looking, discarding the replaced card, or (b) if it is a Jack or Queen drawn from stock, use its power (Jack: swap any two layout cards; Queen: peek at one card) then discard it. Power cards from discard have no power. To end the round: call 'Dacz' instead of drawing; each opponent gets one more turn, then all score.",
      'Scoring example: Lowest total wins. Special values for Kings and certain Face cards depending on the variant. Lowest cumulative score after a set number of rounds (usually 9 or until someone hits 100)..',
